# Meshtastic PowerMon — power-state activity instrumentation
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0

config MESHTASTIC_POWERMON
	bool "Power-state activity monitor (PowerMon)"
	default n
	help
	  Track power-relevant subsystem activity (LoRa RX/TX, wifi, light sleep,
	  Vext, GNSS, ...) as an atomic bitmask, logged on change at INF level and
	  readable over the shell ("powermon"). Intended for bench power
	  characterisation: correlate a measured current draw with what the node is
	  actually doing.

	  Zero cost when disabled — the instrumentation calls compile to no-ops, so
	  the radio/wifi/PM call sites carry no #ifdef. With CONFIG_PM, a PM notifier
	  additionally tracks the ESP32-S3 light-sleep state (atomically, no logging
	  from that constrained context).

	  Raise just this module's verbosity at the bench with
	  "log level dbg meshtastic_powermon" (state changes log at INF by default).
